  "notes": "USAGE:\nMost commonly appears in negative constructions: {容赦|ようしゃ}なく (mercilessly, relentlessly), {容赦|ようしゃ}しない (to show no mercy), {容赦|ようしゃ}ない (merciless). The polite apology phrase ご{容赦|ようしゃ}ください means \"please forgive/excuse\" and appears in formal writing and business communications.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {容赦|ようしゃ}なく: mercilessly, relentlessly\n- {容赦|ようしゃ}しない: to show no mercy\n- {容赦|ようしゃ}ない: merciless, unforgiving\n- ご{容赦|ようしゃ}ください: please forgive, please excuse\n- {容赦|ようしゃ}のない{批判|ひはん}: merciless criticism",
